# Wine ntdll conformance units that must pass through the layer with 0 failures
# (tests/winetest/run_ntdll.cmake, ctest integration.winetest_ntdll on the Windows
# jobs; docs/slices/wt-ntdll.md has the rest, with the failing assertion lines).
#
#   <unit> <minimum number of assertions executed>
#
# A listed unit fails the test when it does not print Wine's summary line (crash or
# timeout), has any failure, or executes fewer assertions than the floor (a unit
# that silently stops early must not pass). Floors are about half of what a unit
# executes today. Add a unit here when it passes; never remove one. (rtlstr and change
# are not here: docs/slices/wt-ntdll.md says why.)
alpc       700
env        300
error      700
large_int  300
path       500
rtlbitmap  200
string     1000000
